# The build context is everything `docker build .` uploads and everything the `build` stage's
# `COPY . .` bakes into a layer. Without this file that includes the local golden/ tree (which
# carries absolute developer paths), the gitignored prompts/ session notes (machine paths, and
# CLAUDE.md's own warning that a local connection string may be scratched there), site-Arch/,
# and the whole .git history. The final image only keeps /app, but the build-stage layers and
# the context transfer keep all of it — so exclude it here rather than trusting multi-stage.
.git
.github
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Gitignored local working state — see tools/golden.sh's header. Never wanted in an image.
golden/
work/
site-Arch/
prompts/

# Session-continuity notes and the plan documents; local-only by design (.gitignore's *.md).
*.md
!README.md

# Build output: rebuilt inside the image anyway, and a host-built bin/ can carry a different
# RID than the container's.
**/bin/
**/obj/
artifacts/
artifacts-test/
